			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=455&amp;sid=53c246549609ce9e4cbb697af62d9b74#455"><img src="templates/subBlack/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Mon Jul 26, 2004 1:01 am<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: What will you do first?</span></td>
				<td valign="top" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=455&amp;sid=53c246549609ce9e4cbb697af62d9b74"><img src="templates/subBlack/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Once you've learned the ropes and built a respectable character that needn't fear pissing himself three steps outside the city gate what will you do first?
<br />
Will you explore? Will you conquer? Will you make new alliances?
<br />

<br />
I think most everyone will probably want to run off on a pioneer quest as soon as possible (the one's where NPCs will remember your name for years to come for discovering their island or saving their town from a dragon, etc) because what could be cooler than staking a claim like that? Although there is also something to be said for being the first person on the server to destroy big baddie and his minions. Even finding a niche and exploiting the hell out of it has its appeal.
<br />

<br />
As for me, I think I'll probably find a nice home and enjoy a sunset. Maybe in a vat of platinum up to my nipples, I haven't really decided yet.</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
